<title>UK: BSkyB gains as Granada says to keep stake.</title>
<headline>BSkyB gains as Granada says to keep stake.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in BSkyB were buoyed on Wednesday as Granada Group said it intends to retain its 10.8 percent stake in the satellite television operator.</p>
<p>The shares were up 9p to 527-1/2p by 0938 GMT.</p>
<p>The media group's chairman Gerry Robinson said on Wednesday that Granada intends to retain its 10.8 percent holding in television broadcaster BSkyB &quot;for the foreseeable future.&quot;</p>
<p>Robinson commented that there was a useful cross-over between the two businesses and that the shareholding had increased in value as BSkyB's share price had risen by over 20 percent in the last six months.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4027</p>
</text>
